  "goodToKnow": "Steigend is the present participle of steigen (to rise), used as an adjective: steigende Preise, steigende Temperaturen, eine steigende Zahl. Its opposites are sinkend or fallend. It takes adjective endings before a noun. The pairing with the verb works the same way as in English: rising prices, falling prices. Don't confuse steigend with steil (steep)."
